{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Root cause:** `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py` used integer floor division (`total // per_page`), so any remainder was ignored. That’s why 101 rows at 10 per page showed 10 pages instead of 11.\n\n**Fix:** Use ceiling division via `(total + per_page - 1) // per_page`, and return `0` when `total <= 0` so empty exports stay consistent with `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py` (which treats `pages == 0` as no last page).\n\n`page_summary` didn’t need changes; it already depends on `num_pages` for `pages` and `last_page_start`. The legacy `old_page_count` wrapper picks up the fix automatically.\n\nAll tests pass (`test_partial_final_page`, `test_exact_multiple`)."}]},"session_id":"71b89e21-8609-4933-9701-fb560edfae69"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":41895,"duration_api_ms":41895,"is_error":false,"result":"Reviewing pagination in `repo/paging.py` and related helpers.\n\n\nFixing `num_pages`: it uses floor division, which drops partial final pages. Replacing it with ceiling division.\n\n\n**Root cause:** `num_pages` in `repo/paging.py` used integer floor division (`total // per_page`), so any remainder was ignored. That’s why 101 rows at 10 per page showed 10 pages instead of 11.\n\n**Fix:** Use ceiling division via `(total + per_page - 1) // per_page`, and return `0` when `total <= 0` so empty exports stay consistent with `page_summary` in `repo/rows.py` (which treats `pages == 0` as no last page).\n\n`page_summary` didn’t need changes; it already depends on `num_pages` for `pages` and `last_page_start`. The legacy `old_page_count` wrapper picks up the fix automatically.\n\nAll tests pass (`test_partial_final_page`, `test_exact_multiple`).","session_id":"71b89e21-8609-4933-9701-fb560edfae69","request_id":"270422e8-4532-447a-9227-7c59ddfc6e7b","usage":{"inputTokens":12452,"outputTokens":1520,"cacheReadTokens":78380,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
